+"""Prized environment: each trial runs in a Prized sandbox.
+
+A Prized sandbox (https://prized.dev/docs/sandboxes) is a Firecracker microVM
+started from a fixed template, not from a Docker image, and its user has no
+root. To run a task's image anyway, this environment unpacks the task's
+prebuilt ``docker_image`` into a root filesystem inside the sandbox (with
+``crane export``; crane is pinned and its checksum checked) and runs every
+command chrooted into it, in unprivileged user namespaces (``_runtime.py``).
+Commands see the image's files, ``ENV``, ``WORKDIR`` and ``USER``, run as root
+(uid 0 of the namespace) or as the requested user, and root can
+``apt-get install``.
+
+Limits, by design of that approach:
+
+- Tasks need ``[environment].docker_image``, pullable without credentials.
+  Building from a Dockerfile (the task's, or a verifier image in
+  ``tests/Dockerfile``) is not supported; build and push the image first. The
+  image's ``ENTRYPOINT`` and ``CMD`` don't run.
+- One id: every user is the same sandbox user underneath, so a non-root user
+  can't be kept away from root's files. Commands for a non-root user (an
+  ``[agent]`` or ``[verifier]`` user, or the image's ``USER``) are refused
+  unless ``allow_unenforced_users`` is set. With it, such a user runs with its
+  own uid, gid and ``$HOME``, and without root's capabilities, but it owns
+  every file root owns, has no supplementary groups, can't ``sudo``, and
+  doesn't see other users' processes (root sees everyone's). Root's ``chown``
+  to other users, its switches to other users (``su``, ``sudo -u``) and
+  setuid/setgid mode bits succeed without effect, as fakeroot does: the command
+  stays root, and programs that check a real user switch (an sshd login,
+  Postfix) fail. Root's group is always 0.
+- The chroot and namespaces are not a security boundary inside the sandbox
+  (the microVM is): no network policies, so ``no-network`` and allowlist
+  tasks are refused. No Docker Compose or GPUs.
+- A command has no time limit of its own: the ``prized`` SDK runs long ones
+  detached and polls them, so they outlive a dropped connection. A trial's
+  sandbox is deleted after ``max_runtime_min`` of running, or
+  ``paused_ttl_min`` after ``stop(delete=False)`` paused it. While the trial
+  runs, a heartbeat keeps it from pausing; one that a crashed Harbor left
+  behind pauses itself after 30 idle minutes, so it stops billing compute, and
+  is deleted ``paused_ttl_min`` later.
+
+Credentials: ``PRIZED_API_KEY``, a key with Sandboxes: Write. See
+``PrizedOptions`` for the ``--ek`` options.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import asyncio
+import base64
+import json
+import logging
+import math
+import os
+import re
+import shlex
+import uuid
+from collections.abc import Awaitable
+from pathlib import Path
+from typing import Any, override
